            <property name="text">
             <string>About the detection</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_detection_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;How the detectors work&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Each detector computes the spectral power of the EEG on sliding windows (Welch's method).&lt;br/&gt;• It flags the windows whose power exceeds its thresholds.&lt;br/&gt;• Several thresholds depend on the power distribution of the selected stages.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;The artifact events&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• The artifacts are added as events to the accessory file of each PSG file (.tsv, .sts or .ent). Snooz creates the .tsv file of an EDF file when it is absent.&lt;br/&gt;• The events with the same group and name are replaced.&lt;br/&gt;• The name of each event ends with @@ and its channel, as in EDFbrowser, for example art_snooz_set1_NREM@@C3.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The documentation of the tool ("Read more!" below) describes each detector and its settings.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
         </layout>
